{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "For my appointment (specs/1.2-features.md §4, UX 2026-11-09; the Reviewer's read). TEMPORARY HOME, as content/toolbox.json: it moves to the app repo's supabase/contracts when the app ports it (decision 99), where it's a PDF made on the device. A summary of the last rangeWeeks weeks, ending today in the saved zone: the number of check-ins (never \"of N days\": that's a missed-days count), the average and small chart for each of mood, sleep, stress and movement (Insights' own rules: a day without a value doesn't count, at least 3 to show), and the starred entries as their date and first line (cut at firstLineChars on a word boundary, with …). An entry's full text only where the person ticks it, none ticked at the start. Never included: neverIncluded. An optional box, What I want to talk about, isn't saved. Nothing is stored or sent by us; the ticks and the box live in the page's memory only. Every string is checked against diagnosisWords (your-week.json's lists), the footer and headings included. Routine (1.4 F, PLAN-routine.md §5, UX 18 Nov): a Routine section with only the items the person opted in (in_appointment); with none, no section (expect null). Per item, in position order, of the range's check-in days on or after its started_on: the share with its tick, as a whole number, halves up (state percent); fewer than rules.routineMinDays such days: state not_enough (\"not enough days yet\"). Never a mood comparison for routine (UX's medication safety ruling). routineCases: {today, weeks, checkIns: [dates], routine: [{id, position, in_appointment, started_on, ticks}], expect}.",
  "rules": {
    "rangeWeeks": [
      2,
      4,
      12
    ],
    "defaultWeeks": 4,
    "firstLineChars": 120,
    "routineMinDays": 5
  },
